{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# What Is Mathematical Modeling?\\n",
        "\\n",
        "This notebook demonstrates the modeling cycle: purpose, variables, parameters, assumptions, equations, simulation, diagnostics, uncertainty, and interpretation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The example model is the bounded-growth equation:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "$$\\\\frac{dx}{dt} = r x \\\\left(1 - \\\\frac{x}{K}\\\\right)$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\\n",
        "import sys\\n",
        "\\n",
        "ARTICLE_ROOT = Path.cwd().parent if Path.cwd().name == 'notebooks' else Path.cwd()\\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(ARTICLE_ROOT / 'python'))\\n",
        "\\n",
        "from what_is_mathematical_modeling.core import LogisticModel, simulate_rk4, sensitivity_oat, monte_carlo_uncertainty\\n",
        "\\n",
        "model = LogisticModel('notebook_baseline', 10.0, 0.35, 100.0, 0.1, 160)\\n",
        "result = simulate_rk4(model)\\n",
        "result.rows[:3], result.rows[-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Sensitivity analysis\\n",
        "\\n",
        "The next cell perturbs key parameters to show how model conclusions depend on assumptions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "sensitivity_oat(model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Monte Carlo uncertainty propagation\\n",
        "\\n",
        "The next cell samples uncertain inputs and propagates them through the model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "mc = monte_carlo_uncertainty(model, n=50, seed=7)\\n",
        "mc[:5]"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "display_name": "Python 3",
